#: ../../../../xonsh/pyghooks.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.pyghooks.XonshConsoleLexer:2 xonsh.pyghooks.XonshLexer:2
msgid "Xonsh console lexer for pygments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/pyghooks.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.pyghooks.XonshConsoleLexer:4
msgid "A xonshcon block is a sequence of lines with the following conventions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/pyghooks.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.pyghooks.XonshConsoleLexer:6
msgid ""
"``@ ...`` — an interactive xonsh command. Tokenised with the ``@ `` (and "
"trailing space) as :data:`Generic.Prompt` so that Sphinx themes / "
"``sphinx_copybutton`` strip the prompt from copy-to-clipboard, leaving just "
"the command text on the clipboard."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/pyghooks.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.pyghooks.XonshConsoleLexer:11
msgid ""
"``>>> ...`` / ``... ...`` — same behaviour for Python interactive prompts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/pyghooks.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.pyghooks.XonshConsoleLexer:14
msgid ""
"A line starting with ``# `` at column 0 — a documented output comment. "
"Tokenised as :data:`Generic.Output` so it is rendered in a distinct (grey) "
"colour and excluded from copy (via ``user-select: none`` on ``.go`` in the "
"Sphinx theme / ``custom.css``). This lets authors annotate *what the command "
"would print* inline while the reader still copies only the code:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/pyghooks.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.pyghooks.XonshConsoleLexer:21
msgid ""
"@ echo 1\n"
"# 1    (output — grey, not copied)\n"
"@ def qwe():\n"
"      print(321)\n"
"  qwe()\n"
"# 321  (output — grey, not copied)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/pyghooks.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.pyghooks.XonshConsoleLexer:30
msgid ""
"A line starting with two leading spaces — a continuation of the previous ``@ "
"`` line (e.g. the body of a ``def``/``for``/...). The first two spaces line "
"up with the character after the ``@ `` prompt and are tokenised as :data:"
"`Generic.Prompt` so they are stripped from copy-paste alongside the real "
"prompts, leaving the body with its true (Python) indentation. Any further "
"whitespace flows into the normal xonsh highlighting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/pyghooks.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.pyghooks.XonshConsoleLexer:38
msgid ""
"Continuation and prompt rules use ``bygroups`` to split the preceding "
"newline off from the prompt token: ``(\\n)(@ |\\. )`` emits ``\\n`` as :data:"
"`Text` (preserved in the clipboard — the two lines stay separated) and ``@ "
"``/``. `` as :data:`Generic.Prompt` (stripped together with its trailing "
"space, so no orphan leading space lands on the next line)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/pyghooks.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.pyghooks.XonshConsoleLexer:45
msgid ""
"The trailing catch-all ``\\n...`` rules keep backwards compat with older "
"xonshcon blocks that have bare output lines at column 0 — any line that is "
"not a prompt, a ``#``-comment, or a 2-space continuation is still tokenised "
"as :data:`Generic.Output`. New documentation should prefer the ``# `` "
"convention so the rendered block is more self-explanatory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/pyghooks.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.pyghooks.XonshConsoleLexer:70 xonsh.pyghooks.XonshLexer:23
msgid ""
"This constructor takes arbitrary options as keyword arguments. Every "
"subclass must first process its own options and then call the `Lexer` "
"constructor, since it processes the basic options like `stripnl`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/pyghooks.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.pyghooks.XonshConsoleLexer:75 xonsh.pyghooks.XonshLexer:28
msgid "An example looks like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/pyghooks.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.pyghooks.XonshConsoleLexer:77 xonsh.pyghooks.XonshLexer:30
msgid ""
"def __init__(self, **options):\n"
"    self.compress = options.get('compress', '')\n"
"    Lexer.__init__(self, **options)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/pyghooks.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.pyghooks.XonshConsoleLexer:83 xonsh.pyghooks.XonshLexer:36
msgid ""
"As these options must all be specifiable as strings (due to the command line "
"usage), there are various utility functions available to help with that, see "
"`Utilities`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/pyghooks.py:docstring of
#: pygments.util.make_analysator.<locals>.text_analyse:2
msgid "A static method which is called for lexer guessing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/pyghooks.py:docstring of
#: pygments.util.make_analysator.<locals>.text_analyse:4
msgid ""
"It should analyse the text and return a float in the range from ``0.0`` to "
"``1.0``.  If it returns ``0.0``, the lexer will not be selected as the most "
"probable one, if it returns ``1.0``, it will be selected immediately.  This "
"is used by `guess_lexer`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/pyghooks.py:docstring of
#: pygments.util.make_analysator.<locals>.text_analyse:10
msgid ""
"The `LexerMeta` metaclass automatically wraps this function so that it works "
"like a static method (no ``self`` or ``cls`` parameter) and the return value "
"is automatically converted to `float`. If the return value is an object that "
"is boolean `False` it's the same as if the return values was ``0.0``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/pyghooks.py:docstring of pygments.lexer.Lexer.add_filter:2
msgid "Add a new stream filter to this lexer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/pyghooks.py:docstring of pygments.lexer.Lexer.get_tokens:2
msgid ""
"This method is the basic interface of a lexer. It is called by the "
"`highlight()` function. It must process the text and return an iterable of "
"``(tokentype, value)`` pairs from `text`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/pyghooks.py:docstring of pygments.lexer.Lexer.get_tokens:6
msgid ""
"Normally, you don't need to override this method. The default implementation "
"processes the options recognized by all lexers (`stripnl`, `stripall` and so "
"on), and then yields all tokens from `get_tokens_unprocessed()`, with the "
"``index`` dropped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/pyghooks.py:docstring of
#: pygments.lexer.Lexer.get_tokens:11
msgid ""
"If `unfiltered` is set to `True`, the filtering mechanism is bypassed even "
"if filters are defined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/pyghooks.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.pyghooks.XonshLexer.get_tokens_unprocessed:2
msgid ""
"Check first command, then call super.get_tokens_unprocessed with root or "
"subproc state."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/pyghooks.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.pyghooks.XonshLexer.get_tokens_unprocessed:5
msgid ""
"Plugin mode (no live session — Sphinx, nbconvert, jupyter) keeps the "
"original strict check here on purpose: ``_command_is_valid`` rejects "
"keywords, so a Python source line like ``from foo import bar`` correctly "
"falls through to root state and is highlighted as Python.  Treating *every* "
"leading token as a valid command would switch the lexer into ``subproc`` "
"state for any input whose first non-whitespace character matches "
"``COMMAND_TOKEN_RE`` (including ``#`` for plain comments), wrecking "
"highlighting for the rest of the file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/pyghooks.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.pyghooks.XonshConsoleLexer.alias_filenames:2
#: xonsh.pyghooks.XonshLexer.alias_filenames:2
msgid ""
"A list of `fnmatch` patterns that match filenames which may or may not "
"contain content for this lexer. This list is used by the :func:`."
"guess_lexer_for_filename()` function, to determine which lexers are then "
"included in guessing the correct one. That means that e.g. every lexer for "
"HTML and a template language should include ``\\*.html`` in this list."
msgstr ""

